# MCP on Cloudflare Workers

When the user is building or changing a Worker MCP server:

- Implement MCP as JSON-RPC over stateless Streamable HTTP at `POST /mcp`. Handle `initialize`, `notifications/initialized` (no body, HTTP 202), `ping`, `tools/list` and `tools/call`.
- Prefer a plain Worker `fetch` handler for a starter. Do not add a framework unless the user asks for one.
- Keep tool input validation in the Worker. Reject bad input before any network call. Return structured errors the client can read.
- Do not store secrets in `wrangler.toml` or commit `.dev.vars`. Use wrangler secrets in production.
- Run `node --test` (or the project's test script) and fix failures before suggesting `wrangler deploy`. A dry-run is fine; a live deploy needs an explicit request.
- Do not implement JavaScript rendering, login walls, or bypasses. If a page is blocked or needs JS, say so and stop.
- Leave authentication and rate limiting out unless the user asks for them. If they do, put checks in the Worker before the tool runs.
